    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NaClO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> is used, even in spacecrafts, to produce <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>.</mo></math> The daily consumption of pure <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> by a person in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>492</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> at <math><mn>1</mn></math> atm, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>.</mo></math> How much amount of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NaClO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo></math> in grams, is required to produce <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> for the daily consumption of a person at <math><mn>1</mn></math> atm, <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>300</mn><mi></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> ? _____</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NaClO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>Fe</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>NaCl</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>FeO</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.082</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>atm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>"
